        "Figure 3: Ranking and Visibility Metrics are straightforward in traditional search engines, which list website sources in ranked order with verbatim content. However, Generative Engines generate rich, structured responses, often embedding citations in a single block interleaved with each other. This makes ranking and visibility nuanced and multi-faceted. Further, unlike search engines, where significant research has been conducted on improving visibility, optimizing visibility in generative engine responses remains unclear. To address these challenges, our black-box optimization framework proposes a series of well-designed impression metrics that creators can use to gauge and optimize their website’s performance and also allows the":
            "图 3：传统搜索引擎按排名顺序列出网站来源及原文摘要，其排名与可见度指标十分直观。然而，生成式引擎会生成丰富且结构化的回复，通常将多个引用相互交织地嵌入同一段落中，这使得排名与可见度变得复杂且多维。此外，如何在生成式引擎回复中优化可见度仍不明确。为应对这些挑战，我们的黑盒优化框架提出了一系列精心设计的曝光度指标，供创作者衡量和优化网站表现，并允许",
        "creator to define their impression metrics.": "创作者自定义其专属曝光度指标。",
        "material to the user query, influence of the citation, uniqueness of the material presented by a citation, subjective position, subjective count, probability of clicking the citation, and diversity in the material presented. We use G-Eval [13], the current state-of-the-art for evaluation with LLMs, to measure each of these sub-metrics.":
            "内容与用户查询的相关性、引用的影响力、引用所呈现内容的独特性、主观位置、主观篇幅、用户点击引用的概率以及呈现内容的多样性。我们采用当前最先进的基于大语言模型的评估方法 G-Eval [13] 来度量上述各项子指标。",
        "2.2.2 Generative Engine Optimization methods for website. To improve impression metrics, content creators must make changes to their website content. We present several generative engineagnostic strategies, referred to as Generative Engine Optimization methods (GEO). Mathematically, every GEO method is a function":
            "2.2.2 面向网站的生成式引擎优化方法。为了提升曝光度指标，内容创作者需要对其网站内容进行调整。我们提出了若干与特定生成式引擎无关的通用策略，统称为生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法。在数学上，每种 GEO 方法均可表示为函数 ",
        "is the initial web content, and": " 表示初始网页内容，而 ",
        "is": " 表示 ",
        "the modified content after applying the GEO method. The modifications can range from simple stylistic alterations to incorporating new content in a structured format. A well-designed GEO is equivalent to a black-box optimization method that, without knowing the exact algorithmic design of generative engines, can increase the website’s visibility and implement textual modifications to":
            "应用 GEO 方法后修改得到的网页内容。这些修改既可以是简单的文风调整，也可以是以结构化形式融入新内容。设计良好的 GEO 方法等价于一种黑盒优化方法：无需知晓生成式引擎的内部算法细节，即可提升网站可见度并针对 ",
        "independent of the exact queries.": " 执行独立于具体查询的文本优化。",
        "For our experiments, we apply Generative Engine Optimization methods on website content using a large language model, prompted to perform specific stylistic and content changes to the website. In particular, based on the GEO method defining a specific set of desired characteristics, the source content is modified accordingly. We propose and evaluate several such methods:":
            "在实验中，我们利用大语言模型对网站内容执行生成式引擎优化方法，通过提示词引导模型对网站进行特定的文风与内容改写。具体而言，依据各 GEO 方法所定义的目标特征对源内容进行相应修改。我们提出并评估了以下九种方法：",
        "1: Authoritative: Modifies text style of the source content to be more persuasive and authoritative, 2. Statistics Addition: Modifies content to include quantitative statistics instead of qualitative discussion, wherever possible, 3. Keyword Stuffing: Modifies content to include more keywords from the query, as expected in classical SEO optimization. 4. Cite Sources & 5. Quotation Addition:":
            "1. 权威化风格（Authoritative）：将源内容的文本风格改写得更具说服力与权威感；2. 补充统计数据（Statistics Addition）：在可行处用定量统计数据替代定性论述；3. 关键词堆砌（Keyword Stuffing）：向内容中塞入更多查询关键词（即传统 SEO 的典型做法）；4. 引用来源（Cite Sources）与 5. 添加引语（Quotation Addition）：",
        "Adds relevant citations and quotations from credible sources, 6.) 6. Easy-to-Understand: Simplifies the language of website, while":
            "添加来自可靠来源的相关引用与直接引语；6. 通俗易懂化（Easy-to-Understand）：简化网站语言表达；",
        "7. Fluency Optimization improves the fluency of website text. 8. Unique Words & 9. Technical Terms: involves adding unique and technical terms respectively wherever possible, These methods cover diverse general strategies that website owners can implement quickly and use regardless of the website content. Further, except for methods 3, 4, and 5, the remaining methods enhance the presentation of existing content to increase its persuasiveness or appeal to the generative engine, without requiring extra content. On the other hand, methods 3,4, and 5 may require some form of additional content. To analyze the performance gain of our methods, for each input user query, we randomly select one source website to be optimized and apply each of the GEO methods separately on the same source. We refer readers to Appendix B.4 for exact prompts and more details on GEO methods.":
            "7. 流畅度优化（Fluency Optimization）：提升网站文本的行文流畅度；8. 独特词汇（Unique Words）与 9. 专业术语（Technical Terms）：分别在适当位置融入独特词汇与专业技术术语。这些方法涵盖了多样化的通用策略，网站所有者无论面对何种网站内容均可快速部署使用。此外，除方法 3、4、5 外，其余方法均通过改善现有内容的呈现方式来增强其说服力或对生成式引擎的吸引力，无需额外补充外部信息；而方法 3、4、5 则可能需要引入适量的新增内容。为分析各方法的性能增益，针对每个输入用户查询，我们随机选取一个源网站作为优化对象，并在同一源网站上分别独立应用每种 GEO 方法。具体提示词及更多细节请参阅附录 B.4。",
        "3 EXPERIMENTAL SETUP 3.1 Evaluated Generative Engine": "3 实验设置  3.1 所评估的生成式引擎",
        "In accordance with previous works [12], we use a 2-step setup for Generative Engine design. The first step involves fetching relevant sources for input query, followed by a second step where an LLM generates a response based on the fetched sources. Due to context length limitations and quadratic scaling cost based on the context size of transformer models, only the top 5 sources are fetched from the Google search engine for every query. The setup closely mimics the workflow used in previous works and the general design adopted by commercial GEs such as you.com, perplexity.ai. The answer is then generated by gpt3.5-turbo model using the prompt":
            "遵循先前的研究工作 [12]，我们采用两阶段架构构建生成式引擎：第一阶段针对输入查询检索相关网页来源，第二阶段由大语言模型基于检索到的来源生成回复。受限于上下文长度及 Transformer 模型随上下文规模呈二次方增长的计算开销，我们对每个查询仅从 Google 搜索引擎获取排名前 5 的网页来源。该设置高度还原了先前工作的工作流以及 You.com、Perplexity.ai 等商用生成式引擎的通用架构。随后，我们使用与先前工作 [12] 相同的提示词调用 gpt-3.5-turbo 模型生成回答 ",
        "same as prior work [12]. We refer readers to Appendix B for more details.": "（详见附录 B）。",
        "Further in Section C.1, we evaluate the same Generative Engine Optimization methods on Perplexity.ai, which is a commercially deployed generative engine, highlighting the generalizability of our proposed Generative Engine Optimization methods.":
            "此外，在第 C.1 节中，我们在已商业化部署的生成式引擎 Perplexity.ai 上评估了相同的生成式引擎优化方法，充分验证了本文所提 GEO 方法的泛化能力。",
        "3.2 Benchmark : GEO-bench": "3.2 基准测试集：GEO-bench",
        "Since there is currently no publicly available dataset containing Generative Engine related queries, we curate GEO-bench, a benchmark consisting of 10K queries from multiple sources, repurposed for generative engines, along with synthetically generated queries. The benchmark includes queries from nine different sources; each further categorized based on their target domain, difficulty, query intent, and other dimensions.":
            "鉴于目前尚无包含生成式引擎相关查询的公开数据集，我们构建了 GEO-bench——一个包含 1 万条查询的基准测试集，汇集了针对生成式引擎改造的多源真实查询以及合成生成的查询。该基准测试集涵盖来自 9 个不同来源的查询，并进一步按目标领域、难度级别、查询意图等维度进行了精细分类。",
        "Datasets: 1. MS Macro, 2. ORCAS-1, and 3. Natural Quesions: [1, 5, 11] These datasets contain real anonymized user queries":
            "数据集构成：1. MS MARCO、2. ORCAS-1 与 3. Natural Questions [1, 5, 11]：这三个数据集包含来自",

        // Page 4: GEO-bench datasets, Tags, Section 3.3, Section 3.4, Section 4
        "t from Bing and Google Search Engines. These three collectively represent the common set of datasets that are used in search engine related research. However, Generative Engines will be posed with far more difficult and specific queries with the intent of synthesizing answers from multiple sources instead of searching for them. To this end, we repurpose several other publicly available datasets: 4. AllSouls: This dataset contains essay questions from \"All Souls College, Oxford University\". The queries in this dataset require Generative Engines to perform appropriate reasoning to aggregate information from multiple sources. 5. LIMA: [20] contains challenging questions requiring Generative Engines to not only aggregate information but also perform suitable reasoning to answer the question (eg: writing a short poem, python code.).":
            "Bing 和 Google 搜索引擎的真实匿名用户查询，共同代表了搜索引擎研究中最常用的基准数据集。然而，生成式引擎往往面临难度更高、更具体的查询，用户期望从多个来源综合生成答案而非仅检索网页。为此，我们改造并引入了多个公开数据集：4. AllSouls：包含牛津大学万灵学院的论述题，要求生成式引擎进行深度推理以聚合多源信息；5. LIMA [20]：包含极具挑战性的指令查询，要求生成式引擎不仅能聚合信息，还能通过推理完成诗歌创作或编写 Python 代码等复杂任务；",
        "6. Davinci-Debtate [12] contains debate questions generated for testing Generative Engines. 7. Perplexity.ai Discover2: These queries are sourced from Perplexity.ai’s Discover section, which is an updated list of trending queries on the platform. 8. ELI-53: This dataset contains questions from the ELI5 subreddit, where users ask complex questions and expect answers in simple, layman’s terms.":
            "6. Davinci-Debate [12]：包含专为测试生成式引擎而生成的辩论类问题；7. Perplexity.ai Discover：采集自 Perplexity.ai 平台的实时热门趋势查询；8. ELI-5：包含来自 Reddit ELI5 社区的问题，用户提出复杂问题并期望获得通俗易懂的解答；",
        "9. GPT-4 Generated Queries: To supplement diversity in query distribution, we prompt GPT-4 to generate queries ranging from various domains (eg, science, history) and based on query intent (eg, navigational, transactional) and based on difficulty and scope of generated response (eg, open-ended, fact-based).":
            "9. GPT-4 生成查询：为进一步丰富查询分布的多样性，我们提示 GPT-4 按不同领域（如科学、历史）、查询意图（如导航型、交易型）以及回复难度与范围（如开放式、事实型）生成补充查询。",
        "Tags. Optimizing website content often requires targeted changes based on the task’s domain. Additionally, a user of Generative Engine Optimization may need to identify an appropriate method for only a subset of queries, considering multiple factors such as domain, user intent, and query nature. To facilitate this, we tag each":
            "分类标签（Tags）：优化网站内容通常需要根据任务所属领域进行有针对性的调整。此外，生成式引擎优化的使用者往往需要综合考量领域、用户意图和查询性质等因素，为特定查询子集挑选最合适的优化方法。为此，我们为每条",
        "query with one of seven different categories. For tagging, we employ the GPT-4 model and manually verify high recall and precision on the test split.":
            "查询标注了七个不同维度的分类标签。我们使用 GPT-4 模型完成自动标注，并在测试集上通过人工核验确认了极高的召回率与精确率。",
        "Overall, GEO-bench consists of queries from 25 diverse domains such as Arts, Health, and Games; it features a range of query difficulties from simple to multi-faceted; includes 9 different types of queries such as informational and transactional; and encompasses 7 different categorizations. Owing to its specially designed high diversity, the size of the benchmark, and its real-world nature, GEObench is a comprehensive benchmark for evaluating Generative Engines and serves as a standard testbed for assessing them for various purposes in this and future works. We provide more details about GEO-bench in Appendix B.2.":
            "总体而言，GEO-bench 涵盖了艺术、健康、游戏等 25 个不同领域的查询，难度横跨简单问题到多维复杂问题，包含信息型、交易型等 9 种查询类型，并具备 7 大分类维度。得益于专门设计的高多样性、大规模体量与真实世界属性，GEO-bench 成为评估生成式引擎的综合基准，为本研究及未来工作提供了标准测试平台。关于 GEO-bench 的更多细节见附录 B.2。",
        "3.3 GEO Methods": "3.3 GEO 优化方法评估设置",
        "We evaluate 9 different proposed GEO methods as described in Section 2.2.2. We compare them with a baseline, which measures the impression metric of unmodified website sources. We evaluate methods on the complete GEO-bench test split. Further, to reduce variance in results, we run our experiments on five different random seeds and report the average.":
            "我们对第 2.2.2 节提出的 9 种 GEO 方法进行了全面评估，并与未修改源网站的基线曝光度指标进行对比。所有方法均在完整的 GEO-bench 测试集上进行评估；此外，为减小结果方差，我们在 5 个不同随机种子下重复实验并报告平均值。",
        "3.4 Evaluation Metrics": "3.4 评价指标",
        "We utilize the impression metrics as defined in Section 2.2.1. Specifically, we employ two impression metrics: 1. Position-Adjusted Word Count, which combines word count and position count. To analyze the effect of individual components, we also report scores on the two sub-metrics separately. 2. Subjective Impression, which is a subjective metric encompassing seven different aspects: 1) relevance of the cited sentence to the user query, 2) influence of the citation, assessing the extent to which the generated response relies on the citation, 3) uniqueness of the material presented by a citation, 4) subjective position, gauging the prominence of the positioning of source from the user’s viewpoint, 5) subjective count, measuring the amount of content presented from the citation as perceived by the user, 6) likelihood of the user clicking the citation, and 7) diversity of the material presented. These submetrics assess diverse aspects that content creators can target to improve one or more areas effectively. Each sub-metric is evaluated using GPT-3.5, following a methodology akin to that described in G-Eval [13]. In G-Eval, a form-based evaluation template is provided to the language model, along with a GE generated response with citations. The model outputs a score (computed by sampling multiple times) for each citation. However, since G-Eval scores are poorly calibrated, we normalize them to have the same mean and variance as Position-Adjusted Word Count to enable a fair and meaningful comparison. We provide the exact templates used in Appendix B.3.":
            "我们采用第 2.2.1 节定义的曝光度指标。具体而言，我们使用两类曝光度指标：1. 位置加权词数（Position-Adjusted Word Count），结合了词数统计与位置权重；为剖析各分量的独立作用，我们也分别报告两个子指标的得分。2. 主观曝光度（Subjective Impression），涵盖七个主观维度：1) 被引用句子与用户查询的相关性；2) 引用影响力，评估生成回复对该引用的依赖程度；3) 引用所呈现材料的独特性；4) 主观位置，从用户视角衡量来源位置的显著程度；5) 主观篇幅，衡量用户感知到的引用内容量；6) 用户点击该引用的可能性；以及 7) 呈现材料的多样性。这些子指标评估了不同侧面，内容创作者可针对性地优化其中一项或多项。每个子指标均遵循类似 G-Eval [13] 的方法使用 GPT-3.5 进行评估：向语言模型提供表单式评估模板及带引用的生成式引擎回复，通过多次采样计算每个引用的得分。鉴于 G-Eval 原始得分校准不佳，我们将其归一化为与位置加权词数具有相同的均值和方差，以便进行公平合理的比较。具体评估模板见附录 B.3。",
        "Furthermore, all impression metrics are normalized by multiplying them with a constant factor so that the sum of the impressions of all citations in a response equals 1. In our discussion, we compare methods by calculating the relative improvement in impression. For an initial generated response":
            "此外，所有曝光度指标均乘以归一化常数因子，使得单次回复中所有引用的曝光度之和等于 1。在分析讨论中，我们通过计算曝光度的相对提升率来对比不同方法。对于由初始来源 ",
        "from sources": " 生成的初始回复 ",
        ", . . . ,": "，…，",
        ", and a modified response": "，以及修改后的回复 ",
        ", the relative improvement in impression": "，每个来源 ",
        "for each source": " 的曝光度相对提升率 ",
        "is measured as:": " 计算公式如下：",
        "The modified response": "其中修改后的回复 ",
        "is produced by applying the GEO method being evaluated to one of the sources": " 是将待评估的 GEO 方法应用于其中一个信息来源 ",
        ". The source": " 后生成的。被选中进行优化的来源 ",
        "selected for optimization is chosen randomly but remains constant for a particular query across all GEO methods.":
            " 是随机抽取的，但在同一查询下对所有 GEO 方法保持一致。",
        "4 RESULTS": "4 实验结果",
        "We evaluate various Generative Engine Optimization methods designed to optimize website content for better visibility in Generative Engine responses, compared against a baseline with no optimization. Our evaluation used GEO-bench, a diverse benchmark of user queries from multiple domains and settings. Performance was measured using two metrics: Position-Adjusted Word Count and Subjective Impression. The former consider word count and citation position in the GE’s response, while the latter computes multiple subjective factors, giving an overall impression score.":
            "我们对旨在优化网站内容以提升其在生成式引擎回复中可见度的多种生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法进行了全面评估，并与未做任何优化的基线进行对比。评估基于涵盖多领域、多场景用户查询的 GEO-bench 基准测试集，采用“位置加权词数”和“主观曝光度”两项核心指标衡量性能：前者综合考量生成式引擎回复中的引用词数与位置，后者计算多项主观因素以给出综合曝光度得分。",

        // Page 5-7: Domain analysis, Multiple websites, Combination of GEO strategies, Qualitative analysis, Related work, Conclusion
        "In Section 4, we presented the improvements achieved by GEO across the entirety of the GEO-bench benchmark. However, in real-world SEO scenarios, domain-specific optimizations are often applied. With this in mind, and considering that we provide categories for every query in GEO-bench, we delve deeper into the performance of various GEO methods across these categories.":
            "在第 4 节中，我们展示了 GEO 在整个 GEO-bench 基准测试集上取得的整体性能提升。然而在真实的搜索优化场景中，往往需要实施特定领域的针对性优化。基于这一考虑，并结合我们为 GEO-bench 中每条查询标注的分类标签，本节深入剖析不同 GEO 方法在各类别下的具体表现。",
        "Table 3 provides a detailed breakdown of the categories where our GEO methods have proven to be most effective. A careful analysis of these results reveals several intriguing observations. For instance, Authoritative significantly improves performance in debatestyle questions and queries related to the “historical” domain. This aligns with our intuition, as a more persuasive form of writing is likely to hold more value in debates. Similarly, the addition of citations through Cite Sources is particularly beneficial for factual questions, likely because citations provide a source of verification for the facts presented, thereby enhancing the credibility of the response. The effectiveness of different GEO methods varies across domains. For example, as shown in row 5 of Table 3, domains such as ‘Law & Government’ and question types like ‘Opinion’ benefit significantly from the addition of relevant statistics in the website content, as implemented by Statistics Addition. This suggests that data-driven evidence can enhance the visibility of a website in particular contexts. The method Quotation Addition is most effective in the ‘People & Society’, ‘Explanation’, and ‘History’ domains. This could be because these domains often involve personal narratives or historical events, where direct quotes can add authenticity and depth to the content. Overall, our analysis suggests that website owners should strive towards making domain-specific targeted adjustments to their websites for higher visibility.":
            "表 3 详细列出了各项 GEO 方法表现最突出的查询类别。深入分析这些结果可以发现诸多有价值的规律：例如，权威化风格（Authoritative）在辩论类问题及“历史”领域查询中显著提升了表现，这与直觉高度吻合，因为更具说服力的行文在辩论场景下往往更具价值；同样，通过“引用来源”（Cite Sources）添加文献出处对事实型问题尤为有效，因为引用为所陈述的事实提供了核验依据，从而增强了回复的可信度。不同 GEO 方法的效果随领域显著变化：例如表 3 第 5 行显示，“法律与政府”领域及“观点类”问题从“补充统计数据”（Statistics Addition）中获益显著，表明数据驱动的论据能在特定语境下大幅提升网站可见度；而“添加引语”（Quotation Addition）在“人物与社会”、“解释说明”及“历史”领域效果最佳，因为这些领域常涉及人物叙事或历史事件，直接引语能显著增加内容的真实感与深度。总体而言，我们的分析表明网站所有者应当根据具体领域对网站进行有针对性的优化调整，以获得更高的可见度。",
        "5.2 Optimization of Multiple Websites": "5.2 多网站协同与竞争优化分析",
        "In the evolving landscape of Generative Engines, GEO methods are expected to become widely adopted, leading to a scenario where all source contents are optimized using GEO. To understand the implications, we conducted an evaluation of GEO methods by optimizing all source contents simultaneously, with results presented in Table 2. A key observation is the differential impact of GEO on websites based on their Search Engine Results Pages (SERP) ranking. Notably, lower-ranked websites, which typically struggle for visibility, benefit significantly more from GEO. This is because traditional search engines rely on multiple factors, such as the number of backlinks and domain presence, which are challenging for small creators to achieve. However, since Generative Engines utilize generative models conditioned on website content, factors such as backlink building should not disadvantage small creators. This is evident from the relative improvements in visibility shown in":
            "随着生成式引擎生态的演进，预计 GEO 方法将被广泛采用，进而形成所有候选源网站内容均使用 GEO 进行优化的局面。为探究这一趋势的影响，我们对同时优化所有源网站内容的场景进行了评估，结果如表 2 所示。一个核心发现是：GEO 对不同搜索引擎结果页（SERP）排名网站的影响存在显著差异。值得注意的是，在传统搜索中难以获得曝光的低排名网站，从 GEO 中获益反而大得多。这是因为传统搜索引擎依赖反向链接数量与域名权重等多重外部因素，小型创作者往往难以企及；而生成式引擎基于网站内容本身调用生成模型，反向链接等因素不再使小型创作者处于劣势。这一点从表 2 所示的可见度相对提升率中得到了充分印证。",
        "Table 2: Visibility changes through GEO methods for sources with different Rankings in Search Engine. GEO is especially helpful for lower ranked websites.":
            "表 2：不同传统搜索排名的信息来源在应用 GEO 方法后的可见度变化。GEO 对排名靠后的网站尤为有益。",
        "This finding highlights GEO’s potential as a tool to democratize the digital space. Many lower-ranked websites are created by small content creators or independent businesses, who traditionally struggle to compete with larger corporations in top search engine results. The advent of Generative Engines might initially seem disadvantageous to these smaller entities. However, the application of GEO methods presents an opportunity for these content creators to significantly improve their visibility in Generative Engine responses. By enhancing their content with GEO, they can reach a wider audience, leveling the playing field and allowing them to compete more effectively with larger corporations.":
            "这一发现凸显了 GEO 作为数字空间民主化工具的巨大潜力。许多传统排名靠后的网站由小型内容创作者或独立企业创建，他们以往很难在搜索结果头部与大型企业抗衡。生成式引擎的到来起初看似对这些小型主体不利，但应用 GEO 方法为这些创作者提供了显著提升生成式引擎回复可见度的契机。通过借助 GEO 增强内容质量，小型创作者能够触达更广泛的受众，拉平竞争起跑线，从而更有效地与大型企业展开竞争。",
        "5.3 Combination of GEO Strategies": "5.3 多种 GEO 策略的组合优化",
        "While individual GEO strategies show significant improvements across various domains, in practice, website owners are expected":
            "尽管单一 GEO 策略已在多个领域展现出显著提升，但在实际应用中，网站所有者通常会同时组合采用多种策略（如结合流畅度优化与统计数据补充）。",
        "Table 3: Top Performing categories for each of the GEO methods. Website-owners can choose relevant GEO strategy based on their target domain.":
            "表 3：各 GEO 方法表现最佳的查询类别。网站所有者可根据目标领域选择相应的 GEO 策略。",
        "4Due to cost constraints, the analysis was conducted on a subset of 200 examples from the test split, and therefore the numbers presented here differ from those in Table 1":
            "注 4：受计算成本限制，本项分析在测试集的 200 个样本子集上进行，因此此处呈现的数值与表 1 存在一定差异。",
        "Figure 4: Relative Improvement on using combination of GEO strategies. Using Fluency Optimization and Statistics Addition in conjunction results in maximum performance. The rightmost column shows using Fluency Optimization with other strategies is most beneficial.":
            "图 4：组合使用多种 GEO 策略的相对性能提升。将“流畅度优化”与“补充统计数据”结合使用可取得最高性能提升；最右侧一列显示将流畅度优化与其他策略联合使用收益最为显著。",
        "Table 4: Representative examples of GEO methods optimizing source website. Additions are marked in green and Deletions in red. Without adding substantial new information, GEO significantly increase visibility.":
            "表 4：GEO 方法优化源网站的代表性示例（绿色代表新增内容，红色代表删减内容）。无需增加大量新信息，GEO 即可显著提升网站可见度。",
        "Addition). The findings underscore the importance of studying GEO methods in combination, as they are likely to be used by content creators in the real world.":
            "补充统计数据）。这些发现凸显了研究组合式 GEO 方法的重要性，因为内容创作者在真实场景中往往会组合使用多种优化策略。",
        "5.4 Qualitative Analysis": "5.4 定性案例分析",
        "We present a qualitative analysis of GEO methods in Table 4, containing representative examples where GEO methods boost source visibility with minimal changes. Each method optimizes a source through suitable text additions and deletions. In the first example, we see that simply adding the source of a statement can significantly boost visibility in the final answer, requiring minimal effort from the content creator. The second example demonstrates that adding relevant statistics wherever possible ensures increased source visibility in the final Generative Engine response. Finally, the third row suggests that merely emphasizing parts of the text and using a persuasive text style can also lead to improvements in visibility.":
            "我们在表 4 中对 GEO 方法进行了定性案例分析，展示了通过极小幅度的改动显著提升来源可见度的代表性示例。每种方法均通过恰当的文本增删来优化源网页：第一个示例表明，仅需补充陈述的引用出处即可大幅提升其在最终回答中的可见度，创作者付出的改动成本极低；第二个示例证明，尽可能补充相关统计数据能够有效确保源网站在生成式引擎最终回复中获得更高曝光；第三个示例则表明，仅通过强调部分文本并采用更具说服力的行文风格，同样能带来可见度的显著提升。",
        "6 GEO IN THE WILD : EXPERIMENTS WITH": "6 真实环境下的 GEO：商用引擎实验",
        "Table 5: Absolute impression metrics of GEO methods on GEO-bench with Perplexity.ai as GE. While SEO methods such as Keyword Stuffing perform poorly, our proposed GEO methods generalize well to multiple generative engines significanlty improve content visibility.":
            "表 5：以 Perplexity.ai 作为生成式引擎时各 GEO 方法在 GEO-bench 上的绝对曝光度指标。关键词堆砌等传统 SEO 方法表现不佳，而本文提出的 GEO 方法在多种生成式引擎上均具备良好的泛化能力并显著提升了内容可见度。",
        "7 RELATED WORK": "7 相关工作",
        "Evidence-based Answer Generation: Previous works have used several techniques for answer generation backed by sources. Nakano et al. [16] trained GPT-3 to navigate web environments to generate source-backed answers. Similarly, other methods [14, 18, 19] fetch sources via search engines for answer generation. Our work unifies these approaches and provide a common benchmark for improving these systems in the future. In a recent working draft, Kumar and Lakkaraju [9] showed that strategic text sequences can manipulate LLM recommendations to enhance product visibility in generative engines. While their approach focuses on increasing product visibility through adversarial text, our method introduces non-adversarial strategies to optimize any website content for improved visibility in generative engine search results.":
            "基于证据的回答生成：先前的研究采用了多种技术来生成有来源支撑的回答。Nakano 等人 [16] 训练 GPT-3 浏览网页环境以生成基于来源的回答；类似地，其他方法 [14, 18, 19] 通过搜索引擎检索信息来源以生成回答。本文统一了上述方法，并为未来改进此类系统提供了通用基准测试集。在近期的一篇工作手稿中，Kumar 和 Lakkaraju [9] 表明特定策略性文本序列可操纵大语言模型的推荐结果以提升产品在生成式引擎中的可见度。不同于他们通过对抗性文本提升产品曝光的做法，本文提出了非对抗性的良性内容优化策略，适用于优化任意网站内容以提升其在生成式引擎搜索结果中的可见度。",
        "Retrieval-Augmented Language Models: Several recent works have tackled the issues of limited memory of language models by fetching relevant sources from a knowledge base to complete a task [3, 6, 15]. However, Generative Engine needs to generate an answer and provide attributions throughout the answer. Further, Generative Engine is not limited to a single text modality regarding both input and output. Additionally, the framework of Generative":
            "检索增强语言模型：近期诸多研究通过从知识库检索相关来源来完成任务，从而缓解语言模型记忆容量有限的问题 [3, 6, 15]。然而，生成式引擎不仅需要生成回答，还必须在整个回答过程中提供准确的来源归属标注；此外，生成式引擎在输入与输出上均不局限于单一文本模态，且生成式",
        "Engine is not limited to fetching relevant sources but instead comprises multiple tasks such as query reformulation, source selection, and making decisions on how and when to perform them.":
            "引擎框架并不仅限于检索相关来源，而是涵盖了查询改写、来源筛选以及决定何时与如何执行这些步骤等多项协同任务。",
        "Search Engine Optimization: In nearly the past 25 years, extensive research has optimized web content for search engines [2, 10, 17]. These methods fall into On-Page SEO, improving content and user experience, and Off-Page SEO, boosting website authority through link building. In contrast, GEO deals with a more complex environment involving multi-modality, conversational settings. Since GEO is optimized against a generative model not limited to simple keyword matching, traditional SEO strategies will not apply to Generative Engine settings, highlighting the need for GEO.":
            "搜索引擎优化（SEO）：在过去近 25 年间，大量研究致力于针对搜索引擎优化网页内容 [2, 10, 17]。这些方法可分为站内 SEO（改善内容质量与用户体验）和站外 SEO（通过外链建设提升网站权重）。相比之下，GEO 面对的是涉及多模态与对话交互的更复杂环境。由于 GEO 针对的是超越简单关键词匹配的生成式模型，传统 SEO 策略不再适用于生成式引擎场景，充分凸显了研究 GEO 的必要性。",
        "8 CONCLUSION": "8 结论",
        "In this work, we formulate search engines augmented with generative models that we dub generative engines. We propose Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) to empower content creators to optimize their content under generative engines. We define impression metrics for generative engines and propose and release GEO-bench: a benchmark encompassing diverse user queries from multiple domains and settings, along with relevant sources needed to answer those queries. We propose several ways to optimize content for generative engines and demonstrate that these methods are capable of boosting source visibility by up to 40% in generative engine responses. Among other findings, we show that including citations, quotations from relevant sources, and statistics can significantly boost source visibility. Further, we discover a dependence of the effectiveness of GEO methods on the domain of the query, and potential of combining multiple GEO strategies in conjunction. We show promising results on a commercially deployed generative engine with millions of active users showcasing the real-world impact of our work. Our work serves as a first step towards understanding the impact of generative engines on the digital space and the role of GEO in this new paradigm of search engines.":
            "在本文中，我们对融合生成式模型的搜索引擎进行了形式化定义，并将其命名为“生成式引擎”（Generative Engines）。我们提出了生成式引擎优化（GEO），赋能内容创作者在生成式引擎时代优化其网页内容。我们定义了面向生成式引擎的曝光度评价指标，构建并开源了涵盖多领域、多场景多样化用户查询及相关网页来源的基准测试集 GEO-bench。我们提出了多种针对生成式引擎的内容优化方法，并证明这些方法能够将生成式引擎回复中的来源可见度提升高达 40%。实验表明，添加文献引用、可靠来源引语以及统计数据能够显著提升来源可见度；同时我们发现了 GEO 方法的效果对查询所属领域的依赖关系，以及联合应用多种 GEO 策略的协同潜力。我们在拥有数百万活跃用户的商用生成式引擎上取得了优异的实验结果，验证了本研究的真实世界影响力。本研究为深入理解生成式引擎对数字生态的影响以及 GEO 在这一搜索新范式中的核心作用迈出了坚实的第一步。",
        "9 LIMITATIONS": "9 局限性讨论",
        "While we rigorously test our proposed methods on two generative engines, including a publicly available one, methods may need to adapt over time as GEs evolve, mirroring the evolution of SEO. Additionally, despite our efforts to ensure the queries in our GEO-bench closely resemble real-world queries, the nature of queries can change over time, necessitating continuous updates. Lastly, while every query in our proposed GEO-bench is tagged and manually inspected, there may be discrepancies due to subjective interpretations or errors in labeling.":
            "尽管我们在包括公开商用平台在内的两个生成式引擎上对所提方法进行了严格测试，但正如传统 SEO 的演进历程一样，随着生成式引擎的不断迭代，GEO 方法也需要随时间动态演进。此外，尽管我们尽力确保 GEO-bench 中的查询高度贴近真实世界查询，但用户查询的形态会随时间推移而变化，需要持续更新维护。最后，尽管 GEO-bench 中的每条查询均经过分类标注与人工抽检，但由于主观理解差异，仍可能存在少量标注偏差。",
        "REFERENCES": "参考文献",

        // Pages 10-16: Appendices A, B, C, D & Figures/Listings/Tables
        "A CONVERSATIONAL GENERATIVE ENGINE": "附录 A 对话式生成式引擎",
        "In Section 2.1, we discussed a single-turn Generative Enginethat outputs a single response given the user query. However, one of the strengths of upcoming Generative Engines will be their ability to engage in an active back-and-forth conversation with the user. The conversation allows users to provide clarifications to their queries or Generative Engine response and ask follow-ups. Specifically, in equation 1, instead of the input being a single query":
            "在第 2.1 节中，我们讨论了给定用户查询输出单次回复的单轮生成式引擎。然而，新一代生成式引擎的核心优势之一在于能够与用户展开多轮交互式对话。多轮对话允许用户针对自身查询或生成式引擎的回复进行澄清并提出追问。具体而言，在公式 (1) 中，输入不再是单一查询 ",
        ", it is modeled as a conversation history": "，而是被建模为由对话历史 ",
        ") pairs. The response": " 组成的序列。此时回复 ",
        "is then defined as:": " 定义为：",
        "(5) where": "(5) 其中 ",
        "is the turn number. Further, to engage the user in a conversation, a separate LLM,":
            " 表示对话轮次。此外，为引导用户持续参与对话，一个独立的大语言模型 ",
        "or": " 或 ",
        ", may generate suggested follow-up queries based on": " 可根据 ",
        ", and": " 与 ",
        ". The suggested follow-up queries are typically designed to maximize the likelihood of user engagement. This not only benefits Generative Engine providers by increasing user interaction, but also benefits website owners by enhancing their visibility. Furthermore, these follow-up queries can help users by getting more detailed information.":
            " 生成推荐追问列表。这些推荐追问通常旨在最大化用户继续交互的概率，这不仅能通过增加用户互动使生成式引擎提供商受益，还能通过提升网站曝光度使网站所有者受益，同时帮助用户获取更详尽的信息。",
        "B EXPERIMENTAL SETUP B.1 Evaluated Generative Engine": "附录 B 实验设置  B.1 所评估的生成式引擎",
        "While the exact design specifications of popular Generative Engines are not public, based on previous works [12], and our experiments, most of them follow 2-step procedure for generating responses. The first step involves fetching relevant sources for input query, followed by a LLM generating response based on the fetched sources. In our setup, we fetch top 5 sources from Google search engine for every query. The answer is generated by gpt3.5-turbo model using a prompt same as prior work [12]. The model is prompted to output an appropriate response for the query, with each sentence cited by one of the 5 sources provided. We sample 5 different answers at temperature=0.7 and top_p=1, to reduce statistical deviations. The exact prompt used is shown in Listing 1.":
            "尽管主流生成式引擎的具体设计规范尚未公开，但根据先前研究 [12] 及我们的实验观察，大多数系统均遵循两阶段回复生成流程：第一步针对输入查询检索相关网页来源，第二步由大语言模型基于检索到的来源生成回复。在本文实验设置中，我们对每个查询从 Google 搜索引擎获取排名前 5 的来源，并使用与先前研究 [12] 相同的提示词调用 gpt-3.5-turbo 模型生成回答，要求模型输出恰当回复并为每个句子标注所提供的 5 个来源之一作为引用。我们在 temperature=0.7、top_p=1 设置下采样 5 个不同回答以减小统计偏差。具体提示词如代码清单 1 所示。",
        "B.2 Benchmark": "B.2 基准测试集详情",
        "Since, currently there is no publicly available dataset containing Generative Engine related queries we curate GEO-bench, a benchmark containing 10K queries from multiple sources repurposed for generative engines along with synthetically generated queries. The benchmark contains queries from nine different sources, each further categorized based on their target domain, difficulty, query intent and other dimensions. The datasets used in constructing the benchmark are: 1. MS Macro & 2. ORCAS-1: contains real anonymized user queries from Bing Search Engine. and 3. Natural Questions: containing queries from Google Search Engine. These three collectively represent the common set of datasets that are used in search engine related research. However, Generative Engines will be posed with far more dofficult and specific queries with intent of synthesizing answer from multiple sources instead of search for them. To this end, we re-purpose several other publicly available datasets: 4. AllSouls: A dataset containing essay questions from “All Souls College, Oxford University”. The queries in the dataset cannot be usually answered from a single source, and requires":
            "鉴于目前尚无包含生成式引擎相关查询的公开数据集，我们构建了包含 1 万条多源改造查询与合成查询的基准测试集 GEO-bench。该基准包含来自 9 个不同来源的查询，并按目标领域、难度、查询意图等维度进行了分类。构建该基准所用的数据集包括：1. MS MARCO 与 2. ORCAS-1（包含来自 Bing 搜索引擎的真实匿名用户查询），以及 3. Natural Questions（包含来自 Google 搜索引擎的查询）。这三者代表了传统搜索引擎研究中最常用的数据集组合。然而，生成式引擎将面临难度更高、更具体的查询，旨在从多个来源综合生成答案而非单纯检索。为此，我们改造了多个公开数据集：4. AllSouls（牛津大学万灵学院论述题数据集），其中问题通常无法由单一来源回答，要求",
        "Listing 1: Prompt used for Generative Engine. The GE takes the query and 5 sources as input and outputs the response to query with response grounded in the sources.":
            "清单 1：生成式引擎所使用的提示词。生成式引擎接收查询与 5 个信息来源作为输入，输出基于这些来源并带有引用标注的回复。",
        "Listing 2: Representative Queries from each of the 9 datasets in GEO-bench":
            "清单 2：GEO-bench 中 9 个数据集各自的代表性查询示例。",
        "Generative Engines to aggregate information multiple sources and perform reasonable reasoning on them. 5. LIMA [20] contains carefully crafted queries and responses for training pretrained language models for instruction following. The queries in the dataset represent a more challenging distribution of queries asked in Generative Engine, and often requires LLM’s creative and technical powress to generate answers (eg: writing short poem, python code.)":
            "生成式引擎聚合多个来源的信息并进行合理推理；5. LIMA [20] 包含精心构建的指令微调查询与回复，代表了生成式引擎中更具挑战性的查询分布，往往需要大语言模型发挥创造力与技术能力来生成答案（例如创作短诗或编写 Python 代码）；",
        "6. Perplexity.ai Discover: These queries are sourced from Perplexity.ai’s, a public Generative Engine, Discover section which is a updated list of trending queries on the platform. These queries represent a real distribution of queries made on Generative Engines.":
            "6. Perplexity.ai Discover：采集自公开生成式引擎 Perplexity.ai 的“发现”板块实时热门查询列表，代表了生成式引擎上的真实用户查询分布。",
        "Tags: Optimizing website content often requires making targeted changes based on the domain of the task. Further, a user of Generative Engine Optimization may need to find an appropriate method for only a subset of queries based on multiple factors, such as domain, user intent, query nature. To this end, we tag each of the queries based from a pool of 7 different categories. For tagging we use GPT-4 model, and manually confirm high recall and precision in tagging. However, owing to such automated system, the tags can be noisy and should not be considered. Detail about each of these queries are presented here and Listing 5":
            "分类标签（Tags）：优化网站内容往往需要根据任务领域进行针对性调整；此外，生成式引擎优化用户可能需要根据领域、用户意图、查询性质等多重因素，为特定查询子集寻找最合适的优化方法。为此，我们从 7 个维度对每条查询进行了分类标注，使用 GPT-4 模型完成自动标注并通过人工核验确认了高召回率与高精确率（各标签维度的详细说明见下文及清单 5）：",
        "Difficulty Level: The complexity of the query, ranging from simple to complex.":
            "难度级别（Difficulty Level）：查询的复杂程度，从简单查询到复杂查询。",
        "Nature of Query: The type of information sought by the query, such as factual, opinion, or comparison.":
            "查询性质（Nature of Query）：查询所寻求的信息类型，例如事实型、观点型或对比型。",
        "Genre: The category or domain of the query, such as arts and entertainment, finance, or science.":
            "领域类别（Genre）：查询所属的学科或领域，例如艺术与娱乐、金融或科学。",
        "Specific Topics: The specific subject matter of the query, such as physics, economics, or computer science.":
            "具体主题（Specific Topics）：查询涉及的具体细分主题，例如物理学、经济学或计算机科学。",
        "Sensitivity: Whether the query involves sensitive topics or not.":
            "敏感度（Sensitivity）：查询是否涉及敏感话题。",
        "User Intent: The purpose behind the user’s query, such as research, purchase, or entertainment.":
            "用户意图（User Intent）：用户提出查询背后的目的，例如学术调研、购买决策或休闲娱乐。",
        "Answer Type: The format of the answer that the query is seeking, such as fact, opinion, or list.":
            "回答类型（Answer Type）：查询所期望的回答格式，例如事实陈述、观点分析或列表归纳。",
        "B.3 Evaluation Metrics": "B.3 评价指标详情",
        "We evaluate all methods by measuring the Relative Improvement in Impression. Specifically, given an initial generated Response":
            "我们通过计算“曝光度相对提升率”来评估所有方法。具体而言，给定初始生成回复 ",
        "s, and a modified response": " 与修改后的生成回复 ",
        "s, we measure the relative improvement in impression of each of the source": "，我们按如下公式度量每个信息来源 ",
        "as:": " 的曝光度相对提升率：",
        "We use the impression metrics as defined in Section 2.2.1. Specifically, we use two impression metrics: 1. Position-Adjusted Word":
            "我们采用第 2.2.1 节定义的曝光度指标，具体包含两项指标：1. 位置加权词数（Position-Adjusted Word",
        "Count which is a combination of word count and position count.": "Count），由词数统计与位置权重组合而成。",
        "To dissect effect of individual components, we also report individual scores on the 2 sub-metrics. 2. Subjective Impression which is a subjective impression metric which is a combination of seven different aspects: Relevance of citation to query, influence of citaiton on response, diversity and uniqueness of information presented, likelihood of followup by the user, perceived rank and amount of information presented in the answer. All these sub-metrics are evaluated using GPT-3.5, using methodology similar to described as in G-Eval [13]. However, since G-Eval scores are ill-calibrated, we need to suitably normalize them for fair and appropriate comparison. We normalize Subjective Impression scores with respect to baseline":
            "为剖析各分量的独立效果，我们也分别报告两个子指标的得分。2. 主观曝光度（Subjective Impression），综合了七个不同维度：引用与查询的相关性、引用对回复的影响力、所呈现信息的多样性与独特性、用户追问的可能性、感知排名以及回答中呈现的信息量。所有这些子指标均遵循类似 G-Eval [13] 的方法使用 GPT-3.5 进行评估。由于 G-Eval 原始得分校准不佳，我们相对于基线",
        "Figure 5: All Tag Categories used for categorizing queries in GEO-bench.":
            "图 5：GEO-bench 中用于对查询进行分类的所有标签类别概览。",
        "scores of Position-Adjusted Word Count to ensure same mean and standard deviation. We list prompts for each of the sub-metrics in Listing 6 7 8 9.":
            "位置加权词数得分对主观曝光度得分进行归一化，以确保二者具有相同的均值和标准差。各子指标的评估提示词见清单 6、7、8、9。",
        "B.4 GEO Methods": "B.4 GEO 优化方法详情",
        "To improve the impression metrics, content creators need to make changes to their websites. To this end, we present several generative engine-agnostic strategies, refered to as Generative Engine Optimization methods (GEO). Mathematically, every GEO method is a function":
            "为了提升曝光度指标，内容创作者需要对其网站内容进行调整。为此，我们提出了若干与具体生成式引擎无关的优化策略，统称为生成式引擎优化方法（GEO）。在数学上，每种 GEO 方法均可表示为函数 ",
        "is the modified website content after applying LEO method. We propose and evaluate a series of methods.":
            " 表示应用 GEO 方法后修改得到的网站内容。我们提出并评估了以下一系列方法：",
        "1: Authoritative: Modifies text style of the source content to be more persuasive while making authoritative claims, 2. Statistics Addition: Modifies content to include quantitative statistics instead of qualitative discussion, wherever possible, 3. Keyword Stuffing: Modifies content to include more keywords from the query, as":
            "1. 权威化风格（Authoritative）：将源内容改写得更具说服力并做出权威论述；2. 补充统计数据（Statistics Addition）：在可行处引入定量统计数据替代定性描述；3. 关键词堆砌（Keyword Stuffing）：向内容中添加更多查询关键词，正如",
        "Figure 6: Evaluation Prompts for different subjective metrics. We use a consistent style for prompts based on the G-Eval method.":
            "图 6：不同主观评价指标的评估提示词（基于 G-Eval 方法采用统一的提示词风格）。",
        "Figure 7: Evaluation Prompts for different subjective metrics. We use a consistent style for prompts based on the G-Eval method.":
            "图 7：不同主观评价指标的评估提示词（基于 G-Eval 方法采用统一的提示词风格）。",
        "Figure 8: Evaluation Prompts for different subjective metrics. We use a consistent style for prompts based on the G-Eval method.":
            "图 8：不同主观评价指标的评估提示词（基于 G-Eval 方法采用统一的提示词风格）。",
        "Figure 9: Evaluation Prompts for different subjective metrics. We use a consistent style for prompts based on the G-Eval method.":
            "图 9：不同主观评价指标的评估提示词（基于 G-Eval 方法采用统一的提示词风格）。",
        "would be expected in classical SEO optimization. 4. Cite Sources & 5. Quotation Addition: Adds relevant citations and quotations from credible sources, 6.) 6. Easy-to-Understand: Simplifies the language of website, while 7. Fluency Optimization improves the":
            "传统 SEO 优化所采取的做法；4. 引用来源（Cite Sources）与 5. 添加引语（Quotation Addition）：添加来自可靠出处的引用与引语；6. 通俗易懂化（Easy-to-Understand）：简化网站语言表达；7. 流畅度优化（Fluency Optimization）：提升",
        "fluency of website text. 8. Unique Words & 9. Technical Terms: involves adding unique and technical terms respectively wherever posssible,":
            "网站文本的行文流畅度；8. 独特词汇（Unique Words）与 9. 专业术语（Technical Terms）：分别在适当位置添加独特词汇与专业术语。",
        "In order to analyse the performance gain of our methods, for each input query, we randomly select one source to be optimized":
            "为分析本文所提方法的性能增益，针对每个输入查询，我们随机选取一个信息来源进行优化，",
        "Figure 10: Prompts for Different Generative Engine Optimization Methods. The prompt takes the web source as input. We mostly use a consistent style for prompts for all the methods.":
            "图 10：不同生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法所使用的提示词。提示词以网页源内容作为输入，且对所有方法采用一致的模板风格。",
        "using all GEO separately. Further, for every method, 5 answers are generated per query to reduce statistical noise in the results.":
            "并分别独立应用每种 GEO 方法。此外，针对每种方法与每条查询均生成 5 个回答，以降低实验结果中的统计噪声。",
        "B.5 Prompts for GEO methods": "B.5 GEO 方法的提示词模板",
        "Here we present prompts used for different Generative Engine Optimization methods. GPT-3.5 turbo was used for all experiments.":
            "本节展示不同生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法所使用的具体提示词。所有实验均采用 GPT-3.5-turbo 模型完成。",
        "C RESULTS": "附录 C 补充实验结果",
        "We perform experiments on 5 seeds, and present results in Table 6":
            "我们在 5 个随机种子下进行了实验，完整结果如表 6 所示。",
        "C.1 GEO in the Wild : Experiments with": "C.1 真实环境下的 GEO：",
        "Deployed Generative Engine": "商用生成式引擎实验",
        "To further reinforce the efficacy of our proposed Generative Engine Optimization methods, we evaluate them on Perplexity.ai a":
            "为进一步验证本文所提生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法的有效性，我们在已部署的商用生成式引擎 Perplexity.ai 上对其进行了评估。",
        "Figure 11: Prompts for Different Generative Engine Optimization Methods. The prompt takes the web source as input. We mostly use a consistent style for prompts for all the methods.":
            "图 11：不同生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法所使用的提示词。提示词以网页源内容作为输入，且对所有方法采用一致的模板风格。",
        "D ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS AND": "附录 D 伦理考量与",
        "REPRODUCIBILITY STATEMENT": "可复现性声明",
        "In our study, we focus on enhancing the visibility of websites in generative engines. We do not directly interact with sensitive data or individuals. While the sources we retrieve from search engines may contain biased or inappropriate content, these are already":
            "在本研究中，我们专注于提升网站在生成式引擎中的可见度，不直接涉及任何敏感个人数据或个体交互。尽管从搜索引擎检索到的网页来源可能包含偏见或不当内容，但这些内容本身已在互联网上",
        "Figure 12: Prompts for Different Generative Engine Optimization Methods. The prompt takes the web source as input. We mostly use a consistent style for prompts for all the methods.":
            "图 12：不同生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法所使用的提示词。提示词以网页源内容作为输入，且对所有方法采用一致的模板风格。",
        "publicly accessible, and our study neither amplifies nor endorses such content. We believe that our work is ethically sound as it primarily deals with publicly available information and aims to improve the user experience in generative engines.":
            "公开可访问，本研究既不会放大也不会背书此类内容。我们认为本研究符合学术伦理规范，因为研究仅处理公开信息并致力于改善生成式引擎的用户与创作者体验。",
        "Regarding reproducibility, we have made our code available to allow others to replicate our results. Our main experiments have been conducted with five different seeds to minimize potential statistical deviations.":
            "在可复现性方面，我们已开源全部代码与数据集以便学界复现实验结果。主要实验均在 5 个不同随机种子下运行，以最大程度减小统计偏差。",
        "Table 6: Performance improvement of GEO methods on GEO-bench. Performance Measured on Two metrics and their sub-":
            "表 6：各 GEO 方法在 GEO-bench 上的性能提升汇总（基于两项核心指标及其子指标进行度量）。",
        "metrics.": "指标。",
        "Figure 13: Prompts for Different Generative Engine Optimization Methods. The prompt takes the web source as input. We mostly use a consistent style for prompts for all the methods.":
            "图 13：不同生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法所使用的提示词。提示词以网页源内容作为输入，且对所有方法采用一致的模板风格。",
        "Fluency Opt.": "流畅度优化",
        "Position-Adjusted Word Count Method Word Position Overall": "位置加权词数  方法  词数  位置  综合得分",
        "Source: It is important to note that The Jaguars have never appeared made an appearance 89.1% in the Super Bowl. However, They have achieved an impressive feat by securing 4 divisional titles to their name. , a testament to their prowess and determination.":
            "源网页示例：值得注意的是，美洲虎队从未亮相超级碗（+89.1%），但他们凭借实力与决心斩获了 4 次分区冠军，取得了令人瞩目的成就。",
        "Table 7: Performance improvement of GEO methods on GEO-bench with Perplexity.ai as generative engine. Compared":
            "表 7：以 Perplexity.ai 作为生成式引擎时各 GEO 方法在 GEO-bench 上的性能提升对比。",
        "Table 7: Performance improvement of GEO methods on GEO-bench with Perplexity.ai as generative engine. Compared to the baselines simple methods such as Keyword Stuffing traditionally used in SEO do not perform very well with often negative performance. However, our proposed methods such as Statistics Addition and Quotation Addition show strong performance improvements across all metrics considered. The best performing methods improve upon baseline by 22% on Position-Adjusted Word Count and 37% on Subjective Impression. The scores demonstrate the high impact of our proposed method directly on":
            "表 7：以 Perplexity.ai 作为生成式引擎时各 GEO 方法在 GEO-bench 上的性能提升。与基线相比，传统 SEO 常用的关键词堆砌等简单方法表现不佳甚至产生负收益；而本文提出的“补充统计数据”与“添加引语”等方法在所有评价指标上均展现出强劲的性能提升，最佳方法在位置加权词数与主观曝光度上分别较基线提升 22% 与 37%，充分证明了本文所提方法直接作用于",
        "the already deployed generative engines.": "已部署商用生成式引擎的显著成效。",
        "Further, GEO introduces a flexible framework for defining visibility metrics tailor-made for generative engines as the notion of visibility in generative engines is more nuanced and multi-faceted than traditional search engines (Figure 3). While average ranking on the response page is a good measure of visibility in traditional search engines, which present a linear list of websites, this does not apply to generative engines. Generative Engines provide rich, structured responses and embed websites as inline citations in the response, often embedding them with different lengths, at varying positions, and with diverse styles. This necessitates the need for visibility metrics tailor-made for generative engines, which measure the visibility of attributed sources over multiple dimensions, such as relevance and influence of citation to query, measured through both an objective and a subjective lens.":
            "此外，GEO 引入了一套专为生成式引擎量身定制的灵活可见度指标定义框架，因为生成式引擎中的可见度概念比传统搜索引擎更加细腻且多维（见图 3）。在呈现线性网站列表的传统搜索引擎中，结果页上的平均排名是衡量可见度的良好指标，但这并不适用于生成式引擎。生成式引擎提供丰富且结构化的回复，并将网站作为行内引用以不同篇幅、不同位置和多样化风格嵌入回复中。因此，亟需专门面向生成式引擎设计的可见度指标，从客观与主观双重维度（如引用与查询的相关性及影响力等）全方位度量归属来源的可见度。",
        "To facilitate faithful and extensive evaluation of GEO methods, we propose GEO-bench, a benchmark consisting of 10000 queries from diverse domains and sources, adapted for generative engines. Through systematic evaluation, we demonstrate that our proposed Generative Engine Optimization methods can boost visibility by up to 40% on diverse queries, providing beneficial strategies for content creators. Among other things, we find that including citations, quotations from relevant sources, and statistics can significantly boost source visibility, with an increase of over 40% across various queries. We also demonstrate the efficacy of Generative Engine Optimization on Perplexity.ai, a state-of-the-art real-world generative engine and demonstrate visibility improvements up to 37%.":
            "为促进对 GEO 方法进行忠实而全面的评估，我们提出了 GEO-bench——一个包含来自不同领域和来源并针对生成式引擎适配的 10,000 条查询的基准测试集。通过系统性实验评估，我们证明所提出的生成式引擎优化方法可在多样化查询上将可见度提升高达 40%，为内容创作者提供了切实有效的优化策略。研究发现，添加文献引用、相关来源引语以及统计数据能够显著提升来源可见度，在各类查询上的增幅超过 40%。我们进一步在当前最先进的真实世界生成式引擎 Perplexity.ai 上验证了 GEO 的有效性，实现了高达 37% 的可见度提升。",
        ". Our benchmark comprises 10K queries divided into 8K, 1K, and 1K for train, validation, and test splits, respectively. We preserve the real-world query distribution, with our benchmark containing 80% informational queries and 10% each for transactional and navigational queries. Each query is augmented with the cleaned text content of the top 5 search results from the Google search engine.":
            "。我们的基准测试集包含 1 万条查询，按 8,000、1,000 和 1,000 划分为训练集、验证集和测试集。我们保持了真实世界的查询意图分布（包含 80% 的信息型查询，以及交易型和导航型查询各 10%），并为每条查询配齐了来自 Google 搜索引擎前 5 个搜索结果的清洗后正文内容。",
        "Table 1 details the absolute impression metrics of different methods on multiple metrics. The results reveal that our GEO methods consistently outperform the baseline across all metrics on GEObench. This shows the robustness of these methods to varying queries, yielding significant improvements despite query diversity. Specifically, our top-performing methods, Cite Sources, Quotation Addition, and Statistics Addition, achieved a relative improvement of 30-40% on the Position-Adjusted Word Count metric and 15-30% on the Subjective Impression metric. These methods, involving adding relevant statistics (Statistics Addition), incorporating credible quotes (Quotation Addition), and including citations from reliable sources (Cite Sources) in the website content, require minimal changes but significantly improve visibility in GE responses, enhancing both the credibility and richness of the content.":
            "表 1 详列了不同方法在多项评价指标上的绝对曝光度得分。结果表明，本文提出的 GEO 方法在 GEO-bench 的所有指标上均稳定优于基线，充分体现了这些方法面对多样化查询时的鲁棒性。具体而言，表现最优的三种方法——“引用来源”（Cite Sources）、“添加引语”（Quotation Addition）和“补充统计数据”（Statistics Addition），在位置加权词数指标上取得了 30%–40% 的相对提升，在主观曝光度指标上取得了 15%–30% 的相对提升。这些方法仅需对网站内容进行极小改动（如补充统计数据、引入可靠引语及添加权威引用），即可显著提升在生成式引擎回复中的可见度，同时增强内容的可信度与丰富度。",
        "Interestingly, stylistic changes such as improving fluency and readability of the source text (Fluency Optimization and Easy-to- Understand) also resulted in a significant visibility boost of 15-30%. This suggests that Generative Engines value not only content but also information presentation.":
            "有趣的是，改善源文本流畅度与可读性等文风优化方法（“流畅度优化”与“通俗易懂化”）同样带来了 15%–30% 的显著可见度提升。这表明生成式引擎不仅看重内容本身，也高度重视信息的呈现方式。",
        "Further, given generative models are often designed to follow instructions, one would expect a more persuasive and authoritative tone in website content to boost visibility. However, we find no significant improvement, demonstrating that Generative Engines are already somewhat robust to such changes. This highlights the need for website owners to focus on improving content presentation and credibility.":
            "此外，鉴于生成式模型通常经过指令微调，人们可能预期在网站内容中采用更具说服力和权威感的语气即可提升可见度；然而实验发现单纯改变语气并未带来显著提升，说明生成式引擎对这类表面改动已具备一定鲁棒性，网站所有者更应专注于改善内容呈现质量与实质可信度。",
        "Finally, we evaluate keyword stuffing, i.e., adding more relevant keywords to website content. While widely used for Search Engine Optimization, we find such methods offer little to no improvement on generative engine’s responses. This underscores the need for website owners to rethink optimization strategies for generative engines, as techniques effective in search engines may not translate to success in this new paradigm.":
            "最后，我们评估了关键词堆砌（即向网站内容塞入更多相关关键词）。尽管该策略在传统搜索引擎优化中被广泛使用，但实验发现它在生成式引擎回复中几乎没有任何正面效果。这凸显了网站所有者重新思考生成式引擎优化策略的必要性——在传统搜索引擎中奏效的技巧未必能迁移至这一新范式。",
        "Table 3 provides a detailed breakdown of the categories where our GEO methods have proven to be most effective. A careful analysis of these results reveals several intriguing observations. For instance, Authoritative significantly improves performance in debatestyle questions and queries related to the “historical” domain. This aligns with our intuition, as a more persuasive form of writing is likely to hold more value in debates.":
            "表 3 详细列出了各项 GEO 方法表现最突出的查询类别。深入分析这些结果可以发现诸多有价值的规律：例如，“权威化风格”（Authoritative）在辩论型问题及“历史”领域查询中显著提升了表现，这与直觉一致，因为更具说服力的行文风格在辩论场景下往往更具价值。",
        "Similarly, the addition of citations through Cite Sources is particularly beneficial for factual questions, likely because citations provide a source of verification for the facts presented, thereby enhancing the credibility of the response. The effectiveness of different GEO methods varies across domains. For example, as shown in row 5 of Table 3, domains such as ‘Law & Government’ and question types like ‘Opinion’ benefit significantly from the addition of relevant statistics in the website content, as implemented by Statistics Addition. This suggests that data-driven evidence can enhance the visibility of a website in particular contexts. The method Quotation Addition is most effective in the ‘People & Society’, ‘Explanation’, and ‘History’ domains. This could be because these domains often involve personal narratives or historical events, where direct quotes can add authenticity and depth to the content. Overall, our analysis suggests that website owners should strive towards making domain-specific targeted adjustments to their websites for higher visibility.":
            "同样，通过“引用来源”（Cite Sources）添加文献出处对事实型问题尤为有效，因为引用为所陈述的事实提供了核验依据，从而增强了回复的可信度。不同 GEO 方法的效果随领域显著变化：例如表 3 第 5 行显示，“法律与政府”领域及“观点类”问题从“补充统计数据”（Statistics Addition）中获益显著，表明数据驱动的论据能在特定语境下大幅提升网站可见度；而“添加引语”（Quotation Addition）在“人物与社会”、“解释说明”及“历史”领域效果最佳，因为这些领域常涉及人物叙事或历史事件，直接引语能显著增加内容的真实感与深度。总体而言，我们的分析表明网站所有者应当根据具体领域对网站进行有针对性的优化调整，以获得更高的可见度。",
        "Table 2. For example, the Cite Sources method led to a substantial 115.1% increase in visibility for websites ranked fifth in SERP, while on average, the visibility of the top-ranked website decreased by 30.3%.":
            "表 2 中。例如，“引用来源”方法使搜索结果页（SERP）排名第五的网站可见度大幅提升了 115.1%，而排名第一的网站平均可见度则下降了 30.3%。",
        "Table 1: Absolute impression metrics of GEO methods on GEO-bench. Performance Measured on Two metrics and their sub-metrics. Compared to baselines, simple methods like Keyword Stuffing traditionally used in SEO don’t perform well. However, our proposed methods such as Statistics Addition and Quotation Addition show strong performance improvements across all metrics. The best methods improve upon baseline by 41% and 28% on Position-Adjusted Word Count and Subjective Impression respectively. For readability, Subjective Impression scores are normalized with respect to Position-Adjusted Word":
            "表 1：各 GEO 方法在 GEO-bench 上的绝对曝光度指标（基于两项核心指标及其子指标度量）。与基线相比，传统 SEO 常用的关键词堆砌等简单方法表现不佳；而本文提出的“补充统计数据”与“添加引语”等方法在所有指标上均取得了显著性能提升，最佳方法在位置加权词数和主观曝光度上分别较基线提升 41% 和 28%。为便于阅读对比，主观曝光度得分已相对于位置加权词数",
        "Count resulting in similar baseline scores.": "进行了归一化处理，使二者具有相近的基线分值。",
        "to employ multiple strategies in conjunction. To study the performance improvements achieved by combining GEO strategies, we consider all pairs of combinations of the top 4 performing GEO methods, namely Cite Sources, Fluency Optimization, Statistics Addition, and Quotation Addition. Figure 4 displays the heatmap of relative improvement in the Position-Adjusted Word Count visibility metric achieved by combining different GEO strategies. The analysis demonstrates that the combination of Generative Engine Optimization methods can enhance performance, with the best combination (Fluency Optimization and Statistics Addition) outperforming any single GEO strategy by more than 5.5%4. Furthermore, Cite Sources significantly boosts performance when used in conjunction with other methods (Average: 31.4%), despite it being relatively less effective when used alone (8% lower than Quotation":
            "组合采用多种策略。为研究组合式 GEO 策略带来的性能增益，我们考察了表现最佳的前 4 种 GEO 方法（引用来源、流畅度优化、补充统计数据、添加引语）的所有两两组合。图 4 展示了组合不同 GEO 策略在位置加权词数指标上取得的相对提升热力图。分析表明，组合使用生成式引擎优化方法能进一步增强效果，最佳组合（流畅度优化 + 补充统计数据）比任何单一 GEO 策略高出 5.5% 以上。此外，“引用来源”与其他方法联合使用时能显著提升表现（平均提升 31.4%），尽管其单独使用时效果相对较低（比“添加引语”低 8%",
        "To reinforce the efficacy of our proposed Generative Engine Optimization methods, we evaluate them on Perplexity.ai, a real deployed Generative Engine with a large user base. Results are in Table 5. Similar to our generative engine, Quotation Addition performs best in Position-Adjusted Word Count with a 22% improvement over the baseline. Methods that performed well in our generative engine such as Cite Sources, Statistics Addition show improvements of up to 9% and 37% on the two metrics. Our observations, such as the ineffectiveness of traditional SEO methods like Keyword Stuffing, are further highlighted, as it performs 10% worse than the baseline. The results are significant for three reasons: 1) they underscore the importance of developing different Generative Engine Optimization methods to benefit content creators, 2) they highlight the generalizability of our proposed GEO methods on different generative engines, 3) they demonstrate that content creators can use our easy-to-implement proposed GEO methods directly, thus having a high real-world impact. We refer readers to Appendix C.1 for more details.":
            "为进一步验证本文所提生成式引擎优化（GEO）方法的有效性，我们在拥有庞大用户群的真实商用生成式引擎 Perplexity.ai 上进行了评估，结果如表 5 所示。与在我们的基准生成式引擎上一致，“添加引语”（Quotation Addition）在位置加权词数指标上表现最佳，较基线提升 22%；“引用来源”与“补充统计数据”等方法在两项核心指标上也分别取得了最高 9% 与 37% 的提升。同时，关键词堆砌等传统 SEO 方法的低效性再次得到印证（表现比基线低 10%）。这一结果具有三方面重要意义：1) 凸显了研发专门面向生成式引擎的优化方法以赋能内容创作者的重要性；2) 验证了本文所提 GEO 方法在不同生成式引擎间的强泛化能力；3) 证明内容创作者可直接应用这些易于落地的 GEO 方法并产生显著的真实世界收益（详见附录 C.1）。",
        "7. Davinci-Debtate [12] contains debate questions generated using text-davinci-003 and sourced from Perspectrum dataset [4]. This dataset were specifically designed for Generative Engines. 8. ELI-5: contains questions from the ELI5 subreddit, where users ask complex questions and expect answers in simple, layman terms. 9. GPT-4 Generated Queries: To further supplement diversity in query distribution and increase Generative Engine specific queries, we prompt GPT-4 to generate queries ranging from various domains (eg: science, history), based on query intent (eg: navigational, transactional), based on difficulty and scope of generated response (eg: open-ended, fact-based). Representative queries from each of the datasets are shown in Figure 2. In total our benchmark contains 10K queries split into 8K,1K,1K train/val/test splits. Every query is tagged into multiple categories gauging various dimensions such as intent, difficulty, domain of query and format of answer type using GPT-4. In terms of query intent, we maintain the real-world query distribution, with our benchmark containing 80% informational queries, and 10% transactional queries and 10% navigational queries [7]. Further, we augment every query with cleaned text content of top 5 search results from Google search engine. Owing to specially designed high benchmark diversity, size, complexity and real-world nature, we believe GEObench is a comprehensive benchmark for evaluating Generative Engines and serves as a standard testbed for evaluating Generative Engines for multiple purposes in this and future works.":
            "7. Davinci-Debate [12]：包含使用 text-davinci-003 基于 Perspectrum 数据集 [4] 生成的辩论问题，专为评估生成式引擎而设计；8. ELI-5：包含来自 Reddit ELI5 社区的问题，用户提出复杂问题并期望获得通俗易懂的解答；9. GPT-4 生成查询：为进一步丰富查询分布多样性并增加面向生成式引擎的查询，我们提示 GPT-4 按不同领域（如科学、历史）、查询意图（如导航型、交易型）以及回复难度与范围（如开放式、事实型）生成查询。各数据集的代表性查询如清单 2 所示。总体而言，我们的基准测试集共包含 1 万条查询，按 8K/1K/1K 划分为训练集、验证集与测试集，并使用 GPT-4 从查询意图、难度、所属领域及回答格式等多个维度对每条查询进行了分类标注。在查询意图上，我们保持了真实世界的分布比例（包含 80% 信息型查询、10% 交易型查询和 10% 导航型查询 [7]），并为每条查询配齐了来自 Google 搜索引擎前 5 个搜索结果的清洗后正文内容。得益于专门设计的高多样性、大规模、高复杂度与真实世界属性，GEO-bench 为本研究及未来工作评估生成式引擎提供了全面而标准的测试平台。",
        "deployed Generative Engine with a large user base. Since perplexity.ai does not allow the user to specify source URLs, we instead provide source text as file uploads to perlexity.ai. We ensure all answers are generated only using the file sources provided. We evaluate all our methods on a subset of 200 samples of our test set. Other experimental procedures are the same as our main results. Results using Perplexity.ai are shown in Table 7. We find, similar to our generative engine Quotation Addition performs the best in Position-Adjusted Word Count with a relative improvement of 22% over the baseline. Further, methods that performed well in our generative engine such as Cite Sources, Statistics Addition show high improvements of up to 9% and 37% on the two metrics. Further, our observations such as the ineffectiveness of traditional methods used in SEO such as Keyword Stuffing are further highlighted, as it performs 10% worse than the baseline. The result underscores the importance of developing different Generative Engine Optimization methods to benefit the content-creators and further highlights that our simple-to-implement proposed methods can be used directly by content-creators, thus having a high real-world impact.":
            "且拥有庞大用户群的商用生成式引擎。由于 Perplexity.ai 不允许用户直接指定外部来源 URL，我们将源网页正文作为文件上传至 Perplexity.ai，并确保所有回答仅基于所上传的文件来源生成。我们在测试集的 200 个样本子集上对所有方法进行了评估，其余实验流程与主实验完全一致，结果如表 7 所示。实验发现，与在我们的基准生成式引擎上一致，“添加引语”（Quotation Addition）在位置加权词数指标上表现最佳，较基线相对提升 22%；“引用来源”与“补充统计数据”等方法在两项指标上也分别取得了最高 9% 与 37% 的显著提升。同时，关键词堆砌等传统 SEO 方法的低效性再次得到凸显（表现比基线低 10%）。这一结果再次印证了研发面向生成式引擎的专属优化方法以造福内容创作者的重要性，并证明本文提出的简洁方法可由内容创作者直接落地应用，产生显著的真实世界价值。"
